applygray.eco.computer.tooltip.0=The core of the computation subsystem.
applygray.eco.computer.tooltip.1=Maximum length of structure: %d
applygray.eco.computer.tooltip.2=The computation subsystem introduces virtual Crafting Processors (vCPUs):
applygray.eco.computer.tooltip.3=The host provides only one vCPU to the ME network at a time, with capacity equal to all currently available bytes in the subsystem.
applygray.eco.computer.tooltip.4=When a user assigns a crafting task to a vCPU, the host automatically adjusts the vCPU's byte allocation to the task's requirements before assigning it to a Threading Core.
applygray.eco.computer.tooltip.5=New vCPUs can be allocated continuously until the total allocated vCPUs reach the max thread count.
applygray.eco.computer.tooltip.6=vCPUs are immediately destroyed when the crafting task completes and all items are returned.
applygray.eco.storage.tooltip.0=The core of the storage subsystem.
applygray.eco.storage.tooltip.1=Maximum length of structure: %d
applygray.eco.storage.tooltip.2=The ECO Storage System is an extensible multiblock storage solution that provides massive storage capacity integrated with your ME Network.
applygray.eco.storage.tooltip.3=It consists of a controller, drives for storage cells, energy cells for power storage, and structural components.
applygray.eco.storage.tooltip.4=The controller determines the tier of the entire system.
applygray.eco.storage.tooltip.5=The Storage Drive holds ECO storage cells; multiple drives can be added to expand storage capacity.
applygray.eco.storage.tooltip.6=The Storage Interface connects the system to your ME Network, and the Heat Sink handles thermal management.
applygray.eco.assembler.tooltip.0=The core of the crafting subsystem.
applygray.eco.assembler.tooltip.1=Maximum length of structure: %d
applygray.eco.assembler.tooltip.2=The ECO Crafting System is an advanced multiblock pattern provider that enables parallel processing of crafting patterns, dramatically increasing crafting throughput.
applygray.eco.assembler.tooltip.3=Unlike the computation system, the crafting subsystem is a pattern provider that can execute multiple patterns simultaneously.
applygray.eco.assembler.tooltip.4=It supports overclocking and active cooling for enhanced performance.
applygray.eco.assembler.tooltip.5=The Pattern Bus holds crafting patterns, and each Worker provides one independent physical execution lane.
applygray.eco.battery.tooltip.0=Energy Buffer for the ME network.
applygray.eco.battery.tooltip.1=Buffer capacity is determined by the installed energy cells.
applygray.eco.battery.tooltip.2=Energy storage starts after the network is connected to an external power supply.
applygray.eco.battery.tooltip.3=High-density energy cells provide power storage for the system.
applygray.eco.battery.tooltip.4=The energy cell tier must match the controller tier.
applygray.eco.memory.tooltip.0=Can drive computation cell.
applygray.eco.memory.tooltip.1=The drivable computation cell tier depends on the computation subsystem host controller.
applygray.eco.memory.tooltip.2=The Computation Drive holds computation cells, providing storage for crafting tasks.
applygray.eco.memory.tooltip.3=More computation cell storage allows larger crafting jobs.
applygray.eco.memory.tooltip.4=The total storage across all cells must meet the crafting job requirements.
applygray.eco.thread.tooltip.0=Threading Core is the main part of the computation subsystem, providing thread count to the host controller.
applygray.eco.thread.tooltip.1=Threads determine the maximum virtual CPUs for the computation subsystem.
applygray.eco.thread.tooltip.2=When destroyed, compressed CPU data will be directly saved to the dropped item.
applygray.eco.thread.tooltip.3=Max thread count +%d
applygray.eco.hyper_thread.tooltip.0=Hyper Thread Core provides more threads.
applygray.eco.hyper_thread.tooltip.1=+10%% bytes required per craft.
applygray.eco.hyper_thread.tooltip.2=Prioritizes normal threads.
applygray.eco.hyper_thread.tooltip.3=Max Hyper Threads: +%d
applygray.eco.parallel.tooltip.0=Parallel Core provides parallel count to the computation subsystem.
applygray.eco.parallel.tooltip.1=Parallel count increases the processing numbers per crafting task for all threading cores.
applygray.eco.parallel.tooltip.2=Max parallel count +%d
applygray.eco.drive.tooltip.0=Can drive storage matrix.
applygray.eco.drive.tooltip.1=The drivable storage matrix tier depends on the storage subsystem host controller.
applygray.eco.energy.tooltip.0=Energy Buffer for the ME network.
applygray.eco.energy.tooltip.1=Buffer capacity: %s AE
applygray.eco.energy.tooltip.2=Energy storage starts after the network is connected to an external power supply.
applygray.eco.worker.tooltip.0=Molecular Assembly Worker is the main part of the crafting subsystem.
applygray.eco.worker.tooltip.1=Molecular Assembly Worker can store 32 crafting jobs, processing 1 crafting job per crafting.
applygray.eco.pattern_bus.tooltip.0=Smart Pattern Bus is the main part of the crafting subsystem.
applygray.eco.pattern_bus.tooltip.1=Each bus can store 63 patterns.
applygray.eco.pattern_bus.tooltip.2=When encoding patterns on the ME Encoding Terminal, you can use the adjacent button to quickly upload them.
